domain SemanticAuthoringDesignRevision4SelfCheck:
  description "Check revision four against the sole revision-three P1 finding without accepting it."
problem P1:
  |
    Determine whether revision four closes provider-timeout request and run transitions
    without choosing pending numeric policy or changing unrelated architecture.
evidence E0:
  |
    The exact English revision-four candidate SHA256 is
    559c8bce9165b51a3aa274c701ee17aee3fe97a96652601cb8b2f7fc71537594.
    Its complete Japanese projection SHA256 is
    b830a65bfe35387e96438eb28774d3dd3505903793e0598c02ec8c1a5949e83b.
evidence E1:
  |
    Revision four section 7.2 requires a current-fence compare-and-set from outstanding
    to timed_out before recovery, retains the receipt and maximum reservation, and
    rejects a late old result for candidate mutation.
evidence E2:
  |
    Revision four section 7.2 gives admitted same-run recovery a distinct request
    identity and recoveryOfRequestId, consumes a strategy change, and records exactly
    one typed recovery basis for a changed transport condition or materially different
    authorized request.
evidence E3:
  |
    Revision four section 7.2 maps zero, consumed, or inadmissible recovery under the
    current fence to failed with provider_transport_unavailable, retained source,
    receipt/accounting, and an owner new-run recipe. A stale handler writes nothing and
    delegates to the current recovery owner's process-or-lease-loss transition.
evidence E4:
  |
    Revision four section 8.3 closes provider request state to reserved, outstanding,
    completed, timed_out, and cancelled and prohibits reopening terminal identities.
evidence E5:
  |
    Revision four section 10 requires the parameterized fixture to prove zero and one
    recovery, exhausted or inadmissible recovery, lost-fence ownership, original late
    result rejection, technical-versus-semantic separation, and absence of an attempt
    elapsed deadline.
premise C1:
  |
    This self-check does not provide fresh independent review or exact owner acceptance.
decision D1 based_on P1, E0, E1, E2, E3, E4, E5:
  |
    Revision four closes the provider-timeout transition identified by the revision-
    three P1 finding and makes its fixture verify rather than invent the state contract.
decision D2 based_on P1, E2, E3, C1:
  |
    Exact timeout values and selection of zero or one recovery remain pending under
    ADR-0032. Keep cc304 suspended and present revision four for fresh REVIEW.
